      "id": "wuthering-heights-s041-p02085",
      "source_en": "1 (p. 49) “She did not yell out”: Emily herself was bitten by a stray dog when she was fifteen. Fearful of contracting rabies, she cauterized the wound with a hot iron and then remained silent about the incident until the danger of infection had passed. Charlotte Brontë used the episode in Shirley (1849), which presents a romanticized portrait of Emily.",
